| background chunk summary, member `lower_band_projection` `pending` | summary work requeues (waits) with reason `member_projection_not_ready` — not concat, not `failed`, not a provider-failure reason |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md:147:| 4 — chunk/compact recovery | background-wait + compact stored-member concat fallback (no model) tests red | TC-4.1a–4.8b pass |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:15:**Vocabulary (this epic settles it).** A **derivation** is the stored result of producing a representation of existing content — a smoothed prompt, a tool-result summary, a turn rendering, a chunk summary. To **derive** is the act. A **derivation type** names which one. A derivation carries a **state**. The code's current `form` / `derived_form` / `FormKind` / `DerivedFormState` names are retired in favor of `derivation` / derivation type / state; the rename is in scope here (Story 0). \"Form\" does not appear in new work.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:24:| `lower_band_projection` | turn | composition | detailed-chunk input; fallback under turn rendering |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:25:| `chunk_summary_detailed` | chunk | inference | detailed band |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:26:| `chunk_summary_brief` | chunk | inference | brief band |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:37:Two things stay clean, one thing stays honest. The **canonical subject** (the message/turn/chunk content) carries no degraded/fallback marker. A **recovered `ready` output** carries no marker either — how it got there (full, floored, or original) is not a distinction the consumer branches on, and there is no \"degraded\" state. But the **derivation record itself keeps its real state and reason**: a `failed` or `blocked` derivation stays `failed`/`blocked` with its failure reason, inspectable through health (Epic 04). Fallback *events* are log-only; derivation *state* is not — the two are different channels. There is no extra field on the subject or the ready output.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:64:- [Chunk Derivation and Compact Recovery](#4-chunk-derivation-and-compact-recovery) — chunk summaries; stored-member concat fallback at compact (no model); corruption blocks. AC: 4.1–4.8\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:98:| A3 | `lower_band_projection` already exists as turn-derivation's second output and the chunk-detailed input | Unvalidated | Tech Lead | Confirm-and-document pass; likely no new work |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:355:### 4. Chunk Derivation and Compact Recovery\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:357:A closed chunk derives two independent summaries — `chunk_summary_detailed` and `chunk_summary_brief` — each with its own state, from the chunk's member turns (via `lower_band_projection`). Smart compact assembles a view from band materials and **never calls a model**. When a needed chunk summary is not ready at compact time, compact does not re-derive it; it falls back to a **deterministic concatenation** of the member content uncompressed — more detail, never a hole. Healing of the summary itself happens out-of-band: the readiness sweep (which runs before compact) requeues transient failures, the background drain produces the real summary, and the next compact uses it. Compact surfaces warnings the user can see and can stop. Only canonical source corruption blocks a compact; missing derivations degrade.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:359:1. A chunk closes; detailed and brief summaries are queued as independent work items\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:360:2. Smart compact assembles bands from chunk summaries and turn renderings\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:366:**AC-4.1:** A closed chunk's detailed and brief summaries are derived as two independent work items with independent states.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:369:  - Given: a chunk closes\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:377:**AC-4.2:** At compact, a chunk summary that is not ready (`pending` or `failed`) resolves through `turns.compactChunkMaterial` to a deterministic stored-member concatenation; compact makes no provider call and does not re-derive the summary.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:384:**AC-4.3:** When a chunk summary still cannot be made ready, compact falls back to a deterministic concatenation of the chunk's member content (uncompressed) rather than leaving a gap.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:387:  - Given: a chunk summary that is not ready at compact time\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:394:  - Given: a compact performs a chunk-summary fallback\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:405:  - Given: multiple missing/failed chunk summaries\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:409:  - Given: canonical source for a chunk's turns is corrupt\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:413:**AC-4.6:** Smart compact performs no provider calls at all; background chunk derivation performs no provider work inside a DB write transaction.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:416:  - Given: a compact over a thread with not-ready chunk summaries, provider spy installed\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:423:  - Given: a compact falls back to concatenation for a chunk\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:425:  - Then: a log entry records the chunk, derivation type, reason, and fallback\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:427:**AC-4.8:** Background chunk-summary derivation behaves differently from compact-time recovery when a member `lower_band_projection` is not ready: because no consumer is waiting, it **requeues and waits** for the input rather than concatenating or failing. It blocks (no progress) only on source corruption of a member; a not-ready member input degrades to a requeue, never a hole or a terminal failure.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:430:  - Given: a chunk summary derives in the background while a member `lower_band_projection` is `pending`\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:432:  - Then: the chunk summary work requeues (waits) rather than concatenating or landing `failed`\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:435:  - When: the background chunk summary attempts to derive\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:458:**AC-5.3:** A fallback *event* is recorded only in the log. The canonical subject (message/turn/chunk content) and any `ready` derivation output carry no degraded/fallback marker. This does not erase derivation state: a `failed` or `blocked` derivation keeps its state and reason on its own record (inspectable per Epic 04) — that is the derivation's state channel, distinct from the fallback-event log channel.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:551:| subjectId | string | no | The subject (message/turn/chunk) id, when relevant |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:587:3. **Background chunk-summary requeue mechanics:** AC-4.8 decides the behavior (requeue/wait on a not-ready member input; block only on member source corruption). Tech design settles the mechanics: requeue backoff, how member source corruption is detected, and how a waiting chunk summary is re-triggered when its member input lands ready.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:588:4. **`lower_band_projection` standalone:** confirm and document it as turn-derivation's second output and the chunk-detailed input; likely no new work, needs a confirm pass.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:642:### Story 4: Chunk derivation and compact recovery\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:644:**Delivers:** independent detailed/brief chunk summaries and a smart compact that regenerates-or-concatenates, warns, is stoppable, and blocks only on source corruption.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:645:**Governing idea:** the cascade instantiated at the chunk/compact level — more detail on fallback, never a hole, corruption is the only stop.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:647:**Boundary / risk notes:** the background chunk-summary requeue behavior is decided (AC-4.8); its mechanics (backoff, re-trigger on member ready, source-corruption detection) are settled in tech design (TD Q3). User-visible warning + stop straddles the LHC/pi-lhc boundary (Flow 5 / TD Q6).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/epic.md:678:- [x] Stories sequence logically (foundation → production floors → turn cascade → chunk/compact cascade → parity)\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts:7:import { chunkBriefV1 } from \"./chunk-brief-v1.js\";\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts:8:import { chunkDetailedV1 } from \"./chunk-detailed-v1.js\";\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts:27:  [chunkDetailedV1.name]: chunkDetailedV1,\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts:28:  [chunkBriefV1.name]: chunkBriefV1,\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts:43:  chunk_summary_detailed: chunkDetailedV1.name,\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts:44:  chunk_summary_brief: chunkBriefV1.name,\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/chunk-detailed-v1.ts:13:export const chunkDetailedV1: PromptTemplate<{\npackages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/chunk-detailed-v1.ts:17:  name: \"chunk-detailed-v1\",\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:63:| Chunk close | Closed chunks queue detailed and brief summaries independently | Story 4 | TC-4.1a, TC-4.1b |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/coverage.md:67:| Background chunk waiting | Not-ready member `lower_band_proje