 make smart compact fall back to deterministic stored-member concatenation without provider calls.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:34:**Objective:** instantiate recovery at chunk and compact level so compact produces usable band material with warnings and blocks only on canonical source corruption.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:37:- Independent `chunk_summary_detailed` and `chunk_summary_brief` work items and states.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:38:- Smart compact recovery through `turns.compactChunkMaterial`.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:42:- Background chunk-summary requeue/wait behavior for not-ready member `lower_band_projection`.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:54:**AC-4.1:** A closed chunk's detailed and brief summaries are derived as two independent work items with independent states.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:57:  - Given: a chunk closes\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:65:**AC-4.2:** At compact, a chunk summary that is not ready (`pending` or `failed`) resolves through `turns.compactChunkMaterial` to a deterministic stored-member concatenation; compact makes no provider call and does not re-derive the summary.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:72:**AC-4.3:** When a chunk summary still cannot be made ready, compact falls back to a deterministic concatenation of the chunk's member content (uncompressed) rather than leaving a gap.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:75:  - Given: a chunk summary that is not ready at compact time\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:82:  - Given: a compact performs a chunk-summary fallback\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:93:  - Given: multiple missing/failed chunk summaries\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:97:  - Given: canonical source for a chunk's turns is corrupt\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:101:**AC-4.6:** Smart compact performs no provider calls at all; background chunk derivation performs no provider work inside a DB write transaction.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:104:  - Given: a compact over a thread with not-ready chunk summaries, provider spy installed\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:111:  - Given: a compact falls back to concatenation for a chunk\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:113:  - Then: a log entry records the chunk, derivation type, reason, and fallback\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:115:**AC-4.8:** Background chunk-summary derivation behaves differently from compact-time recovery when a member `lower_band_projection` is not ready: because no consumer is waiting, it **requeues and waits** for the input rather than concatenating or failing. It blocks (no progress) only on source corruption of a member; a not-ready member input degrades to a requeue, never a hole or a terminal failure.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:118:  - Given: a chunk summary derives in the background while a member `lower_band_projection` is `pending`\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:120:  - Then: the chunk summary work requeues (waits) rather than concatenating or landing `failed`\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:123:  - When: the background chunk summary attempts to derive\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:131:Story 4 owns the chunk and compact recovery boundary. Background chunk-summary derivation waits for member `lower_band_projection` inputs because no consumer is waiting. Compact is a consumer path and never calls a provider; it asks the turns surface for ready summary material or deterministic stored-member concatenation.\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:152:| Background chunk summary | `packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts` |\\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/04-chunk-derivation-compact-recovery/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:154:| Chunk